  "verbalization": "Tepoxalin is shown to interact with the Adenosine receptor A1 through a series of molecular pathways, with the Kappa-type opioid receptor acting as a intermediate target. The evidence suggests that Tepoxalin binds to the Kappa-type opioid receptor, which in turn targets the Adenosine receptor A1. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple compounds that are known to interact with the Adenosine receptor A1, indicating a potential biological mechanism involving receptor modulation. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Tepoxalin in modulating adenosine signaling through the Kappa-type opioid receptor, which may have implications for therapeutic applications targeting adenosine receptor function. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Tepoxalin and Adenosine receptor A1, though further validation through experimental studies would be necessary to confirm the specificity and efficacy of this interaction.",
